## Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js App Router project.

### Changes Made

**1. Installed @vercel/analytics package**
   - Added `@vercel/analytics` as a dependency
   - Used npm to install the package
   - Updated package.json and package-lock.json

**2. Updated app/layout.tsx**
   - Imported `Analytics` component from `@vercel/analytics/next`
   - Added `<Analytics />` component inside the `<body>` tag after `{children}`
   - Also properly added the existing `<SpeedInsights />` component which was imported but not being used

### Modified Files
- `app/layout.tsx` - Added Analytics and SpeedInsights components
- `package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `package-lock.json` - Updated lock file with new dependency

### Implementation Details
The project uses the Next.js App Router pattern with TypeScript. The Analytics component was added to the root layout file (`app/layout.tsx`) which ensures it runs on all pages of the application. The component is placed inside the `<body>` tag after the main content, following Vercel's recommended placement pattern.

Additionally, I noticed that SpeedInsights was already imported but not being used in the layout, so I added it alongside Analytics to resolve the linting warning.

### Verification
- ✅ Build completed successfully with no errors
- ✅ Linter passes with no errors (only pre-existing warning in postcss.config.mjs)
- ✅ TypeScript compilation successful
- ✅ All changes staged with git

The Vercel Web Analytics is now properly configured and will start collecting analytics data when the application is deployed to Vercel.
